Maya (SDK): Quick q — what's our recommended pattern for mapping Redwood API errors into SDK exceptions across languages? Specifically: include request IDs, how to log debug info safely, and streaming mid-stream failures + retries?

Chris (Platform): We set `x-request-id` on responses (and accept it from clients). Best practice: surface request id on every exception as `.request_id` and include it in logs/traces. We also emit an internal trace id `x-rd-request-id` for correlating infra logs.

Maya (SDK): Thinking to create base `ApiError` with fields (status, code, message, request_id, raw_body) and then typed subclasses (`AuthenticationError`, `RateLimitError`, `ServerError`, `StreamInterruptedError`). Thoughts?

Olivia (DevEx): +1. Also include `.retry_after` if the header is present. Keep verbose debug logging off by default; enable via env `REDWOOD_SDK_DEBUG=true` or client option. When debug is on, include `raw_body` but redact tokens/emails. Example python snippet: 

```python
class ApiError(Exception):
    def __init__(self, status, code, msg, request_id=None, raw=None, retry_after=None):
        super().__init__(msg)
        self.status = status
        self.code = code
        self.request_id = request_id
        self.raw = raw
        self.retry_after = retry_after
```

Chris (Platform): Retry guidance: 429 and 5xx -> retry with exponential backoff + jitter. 4xx (except 429 and 409 when idempotency might change handling) -> don't retry. For idempotent operations, encourage `Idempotency-Key` header from clients. Also log `model`, `route`, and hashed `customer_id` (never log raw PII).

Samir (Eng-ML): Streaming quirk — if a stream dies mid-chunk, raise `StreamInterruptedError` with `.partial` containing accumulated tokens/chunks so callers can decide to resume/concat. If the model and route support resumption, include a `resume_cursor` field in the error. Also note that resuming may require rebuilding KV cache; document `preserve_kv_on_resume` behavior (default false).

Maya (SDK): For Node folks — plan to map HTTP errors to classes and attach `requestId` property. Example JS shape?

Olivia (DevEx): Node example: 

```js
class ApiError extends Error {
  constructor({status, code, message, requestId, raw, retryAfter}) {
    super(message);
    this.status = status;
    this.code = code;
    this.requestId = requestId;
    this.raw = raw;
    this.retryAfter = retryAfter;
  }
}
```

Maya (SDK): Good. We'll also include structured debug logs when enabled: `{ts, level, route, request_id, model, shard_id}` and redact anything that looks like an email or API key.

